    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** standing alone as the clear anchor of the lineup. With a dominant score of 77.51, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an ideal matchup against Lambert, and his 10% boost from leading off, combined with a 14% dynamic platoon advantage, makes him our highest-upside play for both power and our critical stolen base category. **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) and **Caleb Durbin** (61.01) provide excellent secondary value; notably, **Caleb Durbin** earns a boost for his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Ober, making him a prime candidate to test the basepaths despite batting in the bottom third of the order.\n\nTactical adjustments are centered on platoon advantages and lineup positioning. **Junior Caminero** (61.15) remains a high-floor start despite a tricky matchup against Weathers, as his raw talent keeps him relevant even when the park factors are not fully in his favor. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** and **Trea Turner** are facing the hurdle of a tough start from Messick (3.36 xERA); while their efficiency scores are dampened, the decision to keep them in the lineup is prioritized by their high-leverage spots (orders #2 and #1) and consistent plate appearances. **Pedro Ramirez** (42.46) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, ultimately sidelined because his lower efficiency compared to the defensive utility of **Caleb Durbin** or the high-ceiling speed of **Hyeseong Kim** made him the odd man out in a crowded middle-infield rotation. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Kazuma Okamoto** closely, as his 55.52 score is teetering; if his mid-order protection falters against Keller, we will need to pivot to bench depth for tomorrow\u2019s series. The organization is also keeping a sharp eye on **Zac Veen**, whose continued residency in Albuquerque is a reminder of our need for reinforcements. Outside of the lineup, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, and **Luis Pena** remain unavailable, ensuring that today\u2019s roster construction is focused entirely on maximizing the 5x5 categories without overextending our season-long game cap management.",
